</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="S6.T5.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Contextual Reinforcement</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T5.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T5.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S6.T5.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">The second attempt reinforces the instruction by providing specific details about the item, creating a stronger connection between the prompt and the required action, thereby reducing ambiguity.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S6.T5.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S6.T5.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
